AI-Driven Prediction and Analysis of Gender-Based Discrimination in Bahrain
Overview

This project investigates gender-based discrimination in workplace and academic environments using Machine Learning (ML), Data Mining, Explainable AI (XAI), Azure AutoML, and Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) technologies. The objective is to identify factors associated with discrimination experiences and provide actionable insights that support equality, diversity, and inclusion initiatives aligned with Bahrain Vision 2030 and the United Nations Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs 4, 5, 8, and 10).

Key Features
Multi-source dataset integration and preprocessing
Arabic-English survey normalization pipeline
Binary classification of discrimination experiences
Class imbalance handling using SMOTE
Multiple supervised learning algorithms:
Logistic Regression
Decision Tree
Random Forest
Gradient Boosting
XGBoost
Hyperparameter optimization using GridSearchCV
Explainable AI through feature importance analysis
K-Means clustering for respondent profiling
Association Rule Mining (Apriori) for pattern discovery
Azure AutoML implementation and deployment
RAG-based chatbot integrated with the deployed model
Cross-platform validation using Python, Orange Data Mining, and Azure
Machine Learning Pipeline
Data Collection
Data Cleaning and Normalization
Missing Value Handling
Feature Encoding
Train-Test Split
Feature Scaling
SMOTE Balancing
Model Training
Hyperparameter Optimization
Model Evaluation
Explainable AI Analysis
K-Means Clustering
Association Rule Mining
Azure AutoML Deployment
RAG Chatbot Integration
Main Findings

The analysis identified several key predictors associated with reported discrimination experiences, including:

Gender Career Influence
Work-Life Satisfaction
Perceived Gender Bias
Workload Distribution
Mentorship Access
Grievance Mechanisms

The best-performing ensemble models achieved strong predictive performance while unsupervised learning techniques revealed hidden respondent profiles and recurring workplace patterns associated with discrimination.

